l is not approval of an implementation or a deployment head.\n\nSecurity: coherent with the repaired archive boundary. J1 preserves the same signed envelope and settles without making a new intent; J2 binds file/diff/interdiff to exact commits and exposes truncation; J3 keeps signing outside an isolated job container and restricts access through a read-only gateway; J4 keeps per-hold scoped credentials and revocation; J5 distinguishes reading from satisfying an obligation. Exact-tree result admission, requested-person review and explicit publication remain part of the journey. These are requirements awaiting implementation evidence, not guarantees certified by this review.\n\nSimplification: appropriate. One bounded real working sprint with a newcomer and fresh agent measures actual acts, refusals, retries, unfinished intentions and stalls. The one-sprint return-to-plain-Git stop rule bounds disruption. Approval carry and act-merging decisions remain deferred until that evidence exists; no additional mechanism or optimization is commissioned.\n\nValidation: original unchanged source citations retain the prior independent pinned-Main checks; new privacy citations, revised dependencies and durable decisions were checked directly. All six relative Markdown links resolve. Whole-tree comparison finds exactly the plan and README changed against Main698, with all other base leaves exact, matching candidate tree, clean shared checkout and clear whitespace. The bounded artifact query has both fresh candidate subjects plus an older broad README subject; that historical subject was not included or retired by this review. No source, tests, dependencies or configuration changed; no test/gate repeat, Source execution, provider operation or push was performed. Full archive, observability, capacity, MVP/J1–J5, evidence-rules, Counter, M1 and measured acceptance outcomes remain owned and open.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3da9c99869